1. Dynamic Memory Allocation -->

Dynamic Memory Allocation is the process of allocating memory at runtime, according to the program's requirements. In C++, dynamic memory is traditionally allocated from the free store (commonly called the heap) using new and released using delete.

Dynamic Memory Allocation वह process है जिसमें program के run time पर आवश्यकता के अनुसार memory allocate की जाती है। C++ में traditionally dynamic memory allocate करने के लिए new और release करने के लिए delete का उपयोग किया जाता है।

Program Start
     ↓
Memory Need
     ↓
Runtime Memory Allocate
     ↓
Data/Object use
     ↓
end work
     ↓
Memory Release

