20. Smart Pointers — Modern C++

Modern C++ में raw new/delete को manually manage करने के बजाय smart pointers preferred हैं।

Main types:

unique_ptr
shared_ptr
weak_ptr

20.1 unique_ptr
unique_ptr provides exclusive ownership of a dynamically allocated object and automatically releases the object when the unique_ptr is destroyed.

unique_ptr dynamically allocated object की exclusive ownership रखता है और unique_ptr destroy होने पर object की memory automatically release कर देता है।

Example
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    unique_ptr<int> p = make_unique<int>(100);

    cout << *p << endl;

    return 0;
}

21. shared_ptr

shared_ptr allows multiple smart pointers to share ownership of the same object.
shared_ptr multiple smart pointers को एक ही object की shared ownership रखने देता है।

Example
#include <iostream>
#include <memory>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    shared_ptr<int> p1 = make_shared<int>(100);

    shared_ptr<int> p2 = p1;

    cout << *p1 << endl;
    cout << *p2 << endl;

    cout << "Owners = " << p1.use_count() << endl;

    return 0;
}

22. weak_ptr

weak_ptr is a non-owning smart pointer that observes an object managed by shared_ptr without increasing its reference count.

weak_ptr shared_ptr द्वारा managed object को observe करता है लेकिन उसकी ownership नहीं लेता।

Main Use

यह विशेष रूप से circular references को avoid करने में useful है।

23. RAII = Resource Acquisition Is Initialization

RAII is a C++ resource-management technique in which resource ownership is tied to an object's lifetime, so the resource is automatically released when the object is destroyed.
RAII C++ की resource-management technique है जिसमें resource को object के lifetime से जोड़ दिया जाता है। Object destroy होने पर resource automatically release हो जाता है।

Flow
Object Created
      ↓
Resource Acquired
      ↓
Object Used
      ↓
Object Destroyed
      ↓
Resource Released

Examples
unique_ptr
shared_ptr
vector
string
File streams

24. Dynamic Memory Allocation Advantages
1. Runtime Allocation
 Memory can be allocated during program execution.
 Program run होने के दौरान memory allocate की जा सकती है।

2. Flexible Size

 Memory size can be determined according to runtime requirements.
 Runtime requirement के अनुसार size तय किया जा सकता है।

3. Useful for Dynamic Data Structures

 Useful for linked lists, trees, graphs, etc.
 Linked List, Tree और Graph जैसी data structures के लिए useful है।

4. Better Control

 Traditional C++ gives programmers direct control over dynamically allocated storage.
 Traditional C++ programmer को dynamically allocated storage पर direct control देता है।

25. Disadvantages / Risks
1. Memory Leak

Memory release करना भूलने पर leak हो सकता है।

2. Dangling Pointer

Freed memory को pointer से access करने की कोशिश unsafe है।

3. Double Delete

Same memory को दो बार delete करना undefined behavior हो सकता है।

4. Manual Management

Raw new/delete में programmer को allocation/deallocation सही तरीके से manage करना पड़ता है।

5. Fragmentation

Long-running programs में अलग-अलग sizes की allocations/deallocations से memory fragmentation हो सकती है।
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    // 1. Different sizes की memory allocate
    int *a = new int[10];
    int *b = new int[20];
    int *c = new int[30];
    int *d = new int[40];

    cout << "Memory allocated." << endl;

    // 2. mid memory release
    delete[] b;
    delete[] d;

    cout << "B and D memory released." << endl;

    // Conceptually memory pattern:
    //
    // [ A ][ FREE ][ C ][ FREE ]
    //
    // Free memory different place 

    // 3.large block 
    int *e = new int[50];

    cout << "Large block allocated." << endl;

    // 4. all memory release
    delete[] a;
    delete[] c;
    delete[] e;

    return 0;
}

